            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a discontinued flavor from a reseller</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Jocko Molk Horchata now appears on Amazon only through a third-party seller at $74.99, well above its old price. Resellers of limited flavors can ship old stock with no easy way to check the date. If a horchata flavor is gone from the brand's own store, buy a current one instead.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every horchata powder is lactose-light</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                LGXNDS Horchata adds non-fat dry milk to its whey isolate, and Primeval Labs adds milk powder and sodium caseinate. Both carry more lactose than a pure isolate. If dairy bothers you, choose Orgain's plant-based version or test a small amount of a whey pick first.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting 'no artificial sweeteners' on the front</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                LGXNDS markets zero artificial sweeteners, yet its Horchata panel lists sucralose. Read the ingredient list, not the bullet points or the front of the tub. Orgain (stevia) and ProDough (stevia and Reb M on its published panels) are the two current horchata powders that avoid sucralose and acesulfame potassium.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Piling cassia cinnamon on a daily shake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Primeval Labs already uses cassia, and horchata shakes invite extra cinnamon on top. Cassia carries much more coumarin than Ceylon. If you add cinnamon every day, use Ceylon, keep cassia to about a quarter teaspoon, and talk to a doctor first if you have liver problems.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per tub instead of per 25 g</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $37.99 tub of Orgain looks cheaper than MusclePharm at $59.49, but MusclePharm costs about $1.14 per 25 g of protein against Orgain's $2.26. Tub sizes here run from 20 to 52 servings, so divide the price by the total protein in the tub before deciding which is cheaper.
              </p>
